WEBVTT

00:00:30.310 --> 00:00:32.460
An Atmospheric Navigation
Bureau alert is in effect.

00:00:32.460 --> 00:00:34.960
No threats observed in the area.

00:00:32.660 --> 00:00:35.330
Special berthing order 
expected in twenty minutes.

00:00:35.330 --> 00:00:38.290
All personnel, be mindful of 
carrier-based craft preparations.

00:00:43.760 --> 00:00:48.650
<i>If the events depicted here bear a 
resemblance to anything you know,</i>

00:00:49.240 --> 00:00:54.800
<i>or the people appearing here bear 
a likeness to anyone you know,</i>

00:00:54.800 --> 00:00:58.320
<i>it is but a fluke of history,</i>

00:00:58.320 --> 00:01:00.030
<i>and an inevitability.</i>

00:02:23.490 --> 00:02:32.000
<b>Legend of the Galactic Heroes</b>

00:02:34.650 --> 00:02:37.140
<i>In the year SE 796,</i>

00:02:37.880 --> 00:02:41.300
<i>there were three opposing 
powers in the Milky Way.</i>

00:02:42.530 --> 00:02:46.440
<i>They were the Goldenbaum Dynasty 
of the Galactic Empire,</i>

00:02:43.850 --> 00:02:46.890
Goldenbaum Dynasty of the Galactic Empire

00:02:51.360 --> 00:02:53.390
<i>the Free Planets Alliance,</i>

00:02:51.440 --> 00:02:54.360
Free Planets Alliance

00:02:56.140 --> 00:02:58.040
<i>and the Dominion of Fezzan.</i>

00:02:56.190 --> 00:02:59.450
Dominion of Fezzan

00:02:59.430 --> 00:03:03.070
<i>The Empire and the Alliance were 
embroiled in a seemingly endless war,</i>

00:03:03.070 --> 00:03:06.790
<i>and the Dominion of Fezzan upheld its 
neutrality as a mere formality.</i>

00:03:07.390 --> 00:03:11.950
<i>The three powers were 
indisputably deadlocked.</i>

00:03:08.870 --> 00:03:13.000
<i>Dominion of Fezzan</i>

00:03:09.580 --> 00:03:13.000
<i>Free Planets Alliance</i>

00:03:10.460 --> 00:03:13.000
<i>Galactic Empire</i>

00:03:23.090 --> 00:03:25.440
Doing some stargazing, Your Excellency?

00:03:30.100 --> 00:03:32.650
Yes. Stars are great.

00:03:36.310 --> 00:03:38.650
You've grown a bit taller, haven't you?

00:03:39.470 --> 00:03:42.950
I'm 190 centimeters, the same as 
two months ago, Your Excellency.

00:03:43.490 --> 00:03:45.620
I don't think I'll grow any taller.

00:03:46.180 --> 00:03:50.090
I suppose seven centimeters 
taller than me is tall enough.

00:03:51.580 --> 00:03:54.550
Anyway, was there something you needed?

00:03:54.550 --> 00:03:57.310
Yes, it concerns the rebel 
force's formation.

00:04:01.110 --> 00:04:04.020
According to reports from 
three of our patrol craft,

00:04:04.020 --> 00:04:08.130
they appear to be approaching from 
three directions, as we expected.

00:04:08.610 --> 00:04:12.010
The enemy's 4th Fleet is 
directly in front of us,

00:04:12.010 --> 00:04:15.840
with an estimated 12,000 ships.

00:04:16.410 --> 00:04:19.100
Distance is approximately 
2,200 light-seconds.

00:04:19.830 --> 00:04:23.910
At our current speed, we should make 
contact in roughly six hours.

00:04:23.910 --> 00:04:26.470
Their army has a total of 40,000 ships...

00:04:26.920 --> 00:04:28.610
That's twice what we have.

00:04:29.170 --> 00:04:33.080
And they're attempting to 
surround us on three sides.

00:04:34.200 --> 00:04:37.060
Our doddering old generals 
must be turning pale now...

00:04:37.060 --> 00:04:39.560
No, perhaps red.

00:04:40.000 --> 00:04:44.010
<b>Episode 1</b>

00:04:40.000 --> 00:04:44.010
<b>In the Eternal Night</b>

00:04:57.520 --> 00:05:01.530
<u>Galactic Imperial Navy Expeditionary Fleet Supreme Flagship</u>
Brünhild

00:05:11.870 --> 00:05:14.910
<u>Galactic Imperial Navy High Admiral
</u>Reinhard von Lohengramm

00:05:15.960 --> 00:05:18.670
<u>Galactic Imperial Navy Captain
</u>Siegfried Kircheis

00:05:18.020 --> 00:05:22.420
Your Excellency, we thank you for this 
opportunity to voice our opinions.

00:05:22.950 --> 00:05:25.150
I know what you want to say.

00:05:25.640 --> 00:05:30.140
You want to warn me that our navy 
is at a disadvantage, correct?

00:05:30.990 --> 00:05:32.790
That is correct, Your Excellency.

00:05:32.790 --> 00:05:34.560
The enemy army doubles ours in number,

00:05:34.560 --> 00:05:37.610
and they're trying to surround 
us on three sides.

00:05:37.610 --> 00:05:40.980
This means the enemy already 
has the edge over us.

00:05:41.580 --> 00:05:44.190
In other words, you're saying we will lose?

00:05:44.530 --> 00:05:49.280
<u>Galactic Imperial Navy
</u>Vice Admiral Staden

00:05:44.620 --> 00:05:46.860
I am not, Your Excellency.

00:05:46.860 --> 00:05:50.200
But it is a fact that we 
are at a disadvantage.

00:05:50.940 --> 00:05:52.670
Please have a look at this.

00:05:54.170 --> 00:05:57.930
Our situation resembles 
the time many years ago

00:05:57.930 --> 00:06:01.570
when our proud Imperial Fleet suffered 
a bitter defeat at the hands

00:06:01.570 --> 00:06:05.100
of the rebel force that called 
itself the Free Planets Alliance.

00:06:05.730 --> 00:06:07.480
The slaughter at Dagon, yes.

00:06:07.480 --> 00:06:10.640
Correct. It was truly a regrettable loss.

00:06:11.820 --> 00:06:16.300
Should we repeat the same 
mistake in this battle,

00:06:16.300 --> 00:06:20.260
it would most certainly trouble 
His Imperial Majesty the Kaiser.

00:06:20.260 --> 00:06:22.560
As such, it is my humble opinion that,

00:06:22.560 --> 00:06:27.100
rather than act in haste, it would be 
wise to make an honorable retreat.

00:06:27.950 --> 00:06:29.910
You speak with eloquence,

00:06:29.910 --> 00:06:32.840
but I cannot agree with your view.

00:06:33.460 --> 00:06:35.830
Retreat is unthinkable.

00:06:36.440 --> 00:06:39.550
But why? Please explain your reasoning.

00:06:41.270 --> 00:06:45.760
Because we have an overwhelming 
advantage over the enemy.

00:06:46.160 --> 00:06:47.110
What?!

00:06:47.110 --> 00:06:48.030
That's...

00:06:52.650 --> 00:06:56.190
The advantage I speak of lies 
in the following points.

00:06:58.200 --> 00:07:00.870
The enemy is divided into three forces,

00:07:00.870 --> 00:07:03.260
but our army is concentrated 
in one location.

00:07:03.260 --> 00:07:05.550
The enemy's total numbers may exceed ours,

00:07:05.550 --> 00:07:09.890
but our army outnumbers each of the 
three forces they've divided into.

00:07:10.560 --> 00:07:13.320
If these are not conditions for 
victory, what else are they?

00:07:15.070 --> 00:07:17.780
We are not in danger of being surrounded.

00:07:17.780 --> 00:07:20.540
We are in the ideal position to defeat 
the enemy's forces one by one.

00:07:21.080 --> 00:07:23.340
You spoke of an honorable retreat,

00:07:23.890 --> 00:07:28.290
but where is the honor in retreating 
without fulfilling the kaiser's orders?

00:07:29.030 --> 00:07:32.810
But that is merely 
Your Excellency's personal belief.

00:07:32.810 --> 00:07:35.680
It does not align with common 
tactical knowledge!

00:07:35.680 --> 00:07:38.760
If you cannot point to an 
instance of success...

00:07:39.150 --> 00:07:43.450
By tomorrow, you will witness an instance 
of success with your own eyes.

00:07:44.020 --> 00:07:45.690
Will that convince you?

00:07:46.140 --> 00:07:47.650
But is victory truly—

00:07:47.650 --> 00:07:48.510
It is possible.

00:07:49.910 --> 00:07:55.310
But only if all of you act in 
perfect accordance with my plan.

00:08:00.000 --> 00:08:02.030
Impertinent brat!

00:08:02.030 --> 00:08:06.760
His sister's relationship with 
the kaiser has made him cocky.

00:08:06.760 --> 00:08:10.270
Such a reckless strategy 
couldn't possibly work!

00:08:11.150 --> 00:08:12.330
Are you sure about that?

00:08:13.630 --> 00:08:18.180
<u>Galactic Imperial Navy Rear Admiral
</u>Adalbert von Fahrenheit

00:08:13.880 --> 00:08:18.470
He is quite a clever man, and I 
thought it was quite a clever idea.

00:08:18.470 --> 00:08:21.180
<u>Galactic Imperial Navy
</u>Rear Admiral Erlache

00:08:18.470 --> 00:08:21.180
<u>Galactic Imperial Navy
</u>Vice Admiral Fogal

00:08:18.470 --> 00:08:21.180
Don't tell me you've been charmed 
by that upstart's indiscretion!

00:08:21.560 --> 00:08:25.400
Fahrenheit, you are still young yourself.

00:08:21.600 --> 00:08:26.020
<u>Galactic Imperial Navy Admiral
</u>Willibald Joachim von Merkatz

00:08:25.970 --> 00:08:27.380
I beg your pardon.

00:08:29.640 --> 00:08:31.120
Was that really wise?

00:08:31.750 --> 00:08:35.420
Leave them. What can they do?

00:08:35.860 --> 00:08:37.390
Don't worry about it.

00:08:38.900 --> 00:08:41.020
They may complain now,

00:08:41.020 --> 00:08:43.410
but in a day, their attitudes will change.

00:08:43.410 --> 00:08:47.560
I'll give that incompetent Staden 
the "instance of success" he wants.

00:08:47.560 --> 00:08:49.440
I'll even frame it for him.

00:08:52.330 --> 00:08:56.300
Care for a drink, Kircheis? 
I have some good wine.

00:08:56.830 --> 00:08:58.840
It's a rare bottle, aged 410 years!

00:08:59.170 --> 00:09:00.610
I'd love to.

00:09:00.610 --> 00:09:01.850
Let's go, then.

00:09:04.700 --> 00:09:06.070
By the way, Kircheis...

00:09:06.070 --> 00:09:07.260
Yes, Your Excellency?

00:09:08.220 --> 00:09:09.560
That's exactly it.

00:09:09.960 --> 00:09:13.820
You don't need to call me 
"Your Excellency" when no one is around.

00:09:13.820 --> 00:09:15.230
How many times have I told you?

00:09:16.300 --> 00:09:18.160
I know that, but still...

00:09:18.910 --> 00:09:21.060
If you know, then do it.

00:09:21.670 --> 00:09:24.270
Once this battle is over 
and we return to Odin,

00:09:24.270 --> 00:09:26.410
you'll be called 
"Your Excellency" yourself.

00:09:28.490 --> 00:09:30.370
You're being promoted to commodore.

00:09:31.170 --> 00:09:32.760
Look forward to it.

00:09:35.290 --> 00:09:36.870
I am honored.

00:09:44.390 --> 00:09:48.400
<u>Free Planets Alliance Army 4th Fleet Flagship
</u>Leonidas

00:09:52.820 --> 00:09:55.440
How credible is that report
from the patrol craft?

00:09:55.720 --> 00:09:58.400
Level A. Possibility of fraud is zero!

00:09:58.760 --> 00:10:01.220
What is the Imperial Army trying to do?

00:10:01.220 --> 00:10:02.860
What are they thinking?

00:10:03.560 --> 00:10:07.530
They know we have them surrounded on 
three sides, but rather than retreat,

00:10:07.530 --> 00:10:10.560
they're actually making 
a move to approach us?

00:10:11.200 --> 00:10:14.130
Their commander has no 
knowledge of tactics!

00:10:11.380 --> 00:10:15.670
<u>4th Fleet Commander
</u>Vice Admiral Pastolle

00:10:14.130 --> 00:10:16.350
Who would fight a battle like this?

00:10:17.230 --> 00:10:21.140
An incomplete encirclement is no 
more than a division of troops.

00:10:21.880 --> 00:10:24.880
That's why it's a perfect chance 
to take them out individually.

00:10:25.830 --> 00:10:29.280
Have we jammed the enemy's data link?

00:10:29.280 --> 00:10:29.930
Yes.

00:10:30.390 --> 00:10:34.000
They weren't expecting us 
to make the first move,

00:10:34.480 --> 00:10:36.840
so it should prove very effective.

00:10:39.010 --> 00:10:41.610
I can just see them running 
around in panic now.

00:10:44.640 --> 00:10:47.880
Kircheis, we will win this war.

00:10:47.880 --> 00:10:50.000
I can see our victory.

00:10:50.000 --> 00:10:51.370
That's all there is to it.

00:10:52.290 --> 00:10:55.290
Your Excellency, what shall we do?

00:10:55.290 --> 00:10:58.760
Send an urgent message to the 
2nd and 6th Fleet commanders!

00:10:58.760 --> 00:11:01.720
Tell them the enemy has engaged 
us, and we need backup!

00:11:02.020 --> 00:11:03.520
There's no answer!

00:11:03.520 --> 00:11:06.600
The enemy's jammed our communications! 
I can't make a connection!

00:11:08.370 --> 00:11:11.560
Dispatch liaison crafts to 
the 2nd and 6th Fleets!

00:11:15.640 --> 00:11:17.640
We're within optical targeting range.

00:11:25.340 --> 00:11:26.250
Feuer!

00:11:35.150 --> 00:11:37.410
Optical signals confirm enemy fire!

00:11:38.100 --> 00:11:40.980
All ships, full shields!

00:11:40.980 --> 00:11:43.920
The enemy jam has severed our data link!

00:11:44.780 --> 00:11:45.920
Shields incomplete!

00:11:55.930 --> 00:11:57.620
Slow to react...

00:11:58.300 --> 00:12:00.480
I guess there are incompetents everywhere.

00:12:00.900 --> 00:12:03.490
Enemy fire is concentrated on 
the center of our front line!

00:12:03.490 --> 00:12:04.810
Damages are severe!

00:12:04.810 --> 00:12:07.690
Data link off! All ships switch to manual!

00:12:07.690 --> 00:12:11.360
Left-flanked 5th Fleet, right-flanked 
7th Fleet, defend our center!

00:12:11.710 --> 00:12:14.300
We'll move forward in the meantime!

00:12:18.960 --> 00:12:22.340
<u>Fahrenheit Fleet Flagship
</u>Heimdall

00:12:19.670 --> 00:12:22.350
Cruising range for carrier-based 
fighter craft achieved.

00:12:22.970 --> 00:12:24.710
Trailing aircraft carriers are ordered

00:12:24.710 --> 00:12:26.790
to launch the Walküre squadron!

00:12:32.260 --> 00:12:33.870
Enemy carrier-based crafts approaching!

00:12:33.870 --> 00:12:36.170
Ready anti-aircraft weaponry!

00:12:49.020 --> 00:12:50.640
Continue the attack!

00:13:01.010 --> 00:13:03.420
<i>This is merely a fluke.</i>

00:13:07.130 --> 00:13:09.360
Transmission from the flagship <i>Brünhild</i>.

00:13:12.850 --> 00:13:16.560
The enemy fleet has lost its capacity 
for organized resistance.

00:13:16.880 --> 00:13:18.070
<i>Good work.</i>

00:13:18.070 --> 00:13:20.020
<i>Isn't there something you'd like to say?</i>

00:13:20.470 --> 00:13:21.470
I don't believe so.

00:13:22.090 --> 00:13:24.710
<i>You're so much more tight-lipped 
than the other admirals.</i>

00:13:25.310 --> 00:13:26.960
<i>There's no need for self-restraint.</i>

00:13:26.960 --> 00:13:29.990
Regardless of how anyone 
behaves, a win is a win.

00:13:29.990 --> 00:13:32.650
I am aware that the victor is always right.

00:13:33.690 --> 00:13:34.650
I see.

00:13:47.170 --> 00:13:49.570
<i>Organized resistance has ceased.</i>

00:13:49.920 --> 00:13:53.130
<i>We're ready to begin combat
with the survivors.</i>

00:13:53.130 --> 00:13:54.170
There's no need.

00:13:54.170 --> 00:13:54.880
<i>What?</i>

00:13:55.300 --> 00:13:58.030
We've only finished one 
third of the battle.

00:13:58.600 --> 00:14:00.800
Leave any surviving forces where they are.

00:14:01.320 --> 00:14:04.900
We need to save our strength 
for the next battle.

00:14:05.240 --> 00:14:06.600
Orders to follow.

00:14:06.600 --> 00:14:08.890
<i>Understood, Your Excellency.</i>

00:14:11.820 --> 00:14:15.280
His attitude has changed a bit.

00:14:15.740 --> 00:14:18.240
Yes, I suppose it would have to.

00:14:19.760 --> 00:14:25.400
By the way, do you think we should strike 
the left or the right fleet next, Kircheis?

00:14:26.340 --> 00:14:29.440
It would be possible to get around 
to the rear flank of either.

00:14:29.440 --> 00:14:31.300
I believe you have made 
up your mind, however.

00:14:31.720 --> 00:14:32.710
True enough.

00:14:34.040 --> 00:14:38.580
The one to the right, the 6th Fleet, 
has smaller numbers.

00:14:39.310 --> 00:14:40.680
Precisely.

00:14:41.150 --> 00:14:43.360
The enemy may have foreseen our plan.

00:14:43.960 --> 00:14:46.140
That is the one thing I 
find slightly concerning.

00:14:46.630 --> 00:14:47.920
No chance of that.

00:14:47.920 --> 00:14:52.110
If they knew, surely they wouldn't 
continue to divide their offensive.

00:14:52.110 --> 00:14:54.480
If their two fleets merged 
as quickly as possible,

00:14:54.480 --> 00:14:58.460
they would have a vast advantage over us.

00:14:59.060 --> 00:15:02.000
It proves they haven't yet 
figured out our intentions.

00:15:03.380 --> 00:15:06.990
We'll go around to the right rear flank 
of the 6th Fleet and attack.

00:15:07.400 --> 00:15:09.200
How long will it take?

00:15:09.200 --> 00:15:10.580
No more than four hours.

00:15:11.390 --> 00:15:14.040
You already had it all 
worked out, didn't you?

00:15:19.460 --> 00:15:24.230
Order all fleets to attack the enemy's 
6th Fleet from the right rear flank.

00:15:25.890 --> 00:15:27.430
Understood.

00:15:37.850 --> 00:15:40.140
From four-thirty?

00:15:37.870 --> 00:15:40.870
<u>6th Fleet Flagship
</u>Pergamonn - Officers' Dining Hall

00:15:40.140 --> 00:15:40.870
Yes, sir.

00:15:40.870 --> 00:15:45.350
I see. And which four-thirty? 
Morning or afternoon?

00:15:41.080 --> 00:15:45.170
<u>6th Fleet Commander
</u>Vice Admiral Moore

00:15:45.960 --> 00:15:47.550
<u>6th Fleet Staff Officer
</u>Lieutenant Commander Jean Robert Lapp

00:15:46.130 --> 00:15:47.550
It is undoubtedly the enemy, sir.

00:15:50.730 --> 00:15:55.500
It can't be. The enemy is fighting 
the 4th Fleet right now.

00:15:55.500 --> 00:15:58.190
We're rushing to the battle as we speak.

00:15:58.190 --> 00:16:02.040
There's no doubt the 2nd Fleet 
is doing the same thing.

00:16:02.040 --> 00:16:05.520
Then we can attack the 
enemy from both sides.

00:16:05.520 --> 00:16:07.690
We have every opportunity to win.

00:16:07.690 --> 00:16:10.090
No, we <i>will</i> win.

00:16:10.090 --> 00:16:11.620
The situation makes that clear.

00:16:11.620 --> 00:16:15.490
But, Your Excellency, couldn't the 
enemy have moved the battlefield?

00:16:15.490 --> 00:16:18.250
And left the 4th Fleet?

00:16:18.250 --> 00:16:20.280
It pains me to say this,

00:16:20.280 --> 00:16:24.240
but I believe the 4th Fleet 
has already been defeated.

00:16:24.240 --> 00:16:28.370
That's a very bold, very unpleasant 
guess, Lieutenant Commander Lapp.

00:16:28.370 --> 00:16:32.340
We must rendezvous with the 
2nd Fleet, and then—

00:16:42.020 --> 00:16:44.560
<u>6th Fleet Flagship
</u>Pergamon

00:16:53.060 --> 00:16:54.900
Enemy attack from the right rear flank!

00:16:54.900 --> 00:16:56.690
Switch to manual operation!

00:16:56.690 --> 00:16:58.100
All ships, turn around!

00:16:58.100 --> 00:17:01.850
Your Excellency, turning around 
will only create chaos!

00:17:03.910 --> 00:17:07.240
I believe we should move ahead at 
full speed in a clockwise direction

00:17:07.240 --> 00:17:11.040
so that we can come around 
behind the enemy.

00:17:11.040 --> 00:17:14.050
Most of our men will have 
been taken out by then!

00:17:14.050 --> 00:17:15.430
We will turn around and strike!

00:17:15.430 --> 00:17:16.190
But—

00:17:16.190 --> 00:17:17.460
Shut up!

00:17:29.810 --> 00:17:32.110
<u>Merkatz Fleet Flagship
</u>Minerva

00:17:33.120 --> 00:17:37.010
Looks like that youngster didn't 
just get lucky after all.

00:17:38.810 --> 00:17:41.240
"Old soldiers just fade away," then?

00:17:50.540 --> 00:17:52.490
Surveillance system showing damage!

00:17:52.490 --> 00:17:54.060
Unable to restore monitors!

00:17:57.900 --> 00:18:00.590
Halt the jamming and send them a message.

00:18:00.990 --> 00:18:02.650
Transmission from the enemy flagship!

00:18:02.650 --> 00:18:05.750
"Surrender. You will be shown mercy."

00:18:08.870 --> 00:18:11.070
Release the bridge from its armor.

00:18:11.070 --> 00:18:13.230
I want to see them with my 
own eyes and fight back.

00:18:13.230 --> 00:18:13.850
But—

00:18:13.850 --> 00:18:15.980
Surrender, you say?

00:18:16.650 --> 00:18:21.570
No, I may be incompetent, 
but I will not be a coward.

00:18:28.940 --> 00:18:30.010
No response.

00:18:31.000 --> 00:18:32.080
Sink them.

00:18:34.640 --> 00:18:37.940
Shields at maximum output! Return fire!

00:18:37.940 --> 00:18:40.470
The enemy has fired 
armor-piercing ammunition!

00:18:54.380 --> 00:18:57.530
Those without skill are destined to fall.

00:18:57.530 --> 00:18:58.910
This is a given.

00:19:00.240 --> 00:19:02.320
<i>Report from our patrol craft.</i>

00:19:02.320 --> 00:19:08.010
<i>The enemy's 2nd Fleet has left the 
battle sector to aid the 4th Fleet.</i>

00:19:08.010 --> 00:19:12.660
<i>We would like to continue our 
advance and attack the 2nd Fleet.</i>

00:19:13.490 --> 00:19:14.710
Very well.

00:19:14.710 --> 00:19:18.170
All fleets will proceed to annihilate 
the enemy's 2nd Fleet.

00:19:25.850 --> 00:19:27.950
The 2nd Fleet is directly ahead of us!

00:19:29.450 --> 00:19:30.170
Feuer.

00:19:30.430 --> 00:19:31.190
Feuer.

00:19:31.410 --> 00:19:32.420
Feuer.

00:19:56.290 --> 00:19:58.470
The enemy craft is hit!

00:20:00.400 --> 00:20:02.920
I do hope we will be able 
to annihilate them all.

00:20:03.660 --> 00:20:06.190
You really are a worrywart, aren't you?

00:20:06.850 --> 00:20:09.150
Do you have such difficulty trusting me?

00:20:09.150 --> 00:20:12.650
I have never once doubted you.

00:20:12.650 --> 00:20:16.190
It's just that, at times, I am afraid.

00:20:16.190 --> 00:20:20.720
What if the enemy has someone extraordinary 
on their side, like we have you?

00:20:21.780 --> 00:20:25.000
You think of the strangest 
things, Kircheis.

00:20:25.680 --> 00:20:29.150
If someone like that were to appear,

00:20:29.150 --> 00:20:31.380
I would love to fight them once.

00:20:31.380 --> 00:20:35.210
And if possible, I'd like 
to see them face-to-face.

00:20:35.730 --> 00:20:37.820
I'm sure we'd have much to talk about.

00:20:38.360 --> 00:20:39.930
Analyzing enemy transmission.

00:20:39.930 --> 00:20:42.040
I believe it to be directed to all fleets.

00:20:43.020 --> 00:20:44.000
Play it.

00:20:44.690 --> 00:20:49.880
<i>I am Commodore Yang Wen-li, deputy 
staff officer to Commander Paetta.</i>

00:20:50.370 --> 00:20:52.520
<i>Our flagship <i>Patoroklos</i> has been hit,</i>

00:20:52.520 --> 00:20:55.270
<i>and Commander Paetta is gravely injured.</i>

00:20:55.750 --> 00:21:00.150
<i>Per the commander's orders, I will 
take over command of all fleets.</i>

00:21:00.980 --> 00:21:04.880
<i>Do not worry. Obey my orders, 
and you will be saved.</i>

00:21:05.680 --> 00:21:09.750
<i>Those who wish to survive, 
remain calm and follow my directions.</i>

00:21:10.630 --> 00:21:13.420
<i>My squadron is losing the 
battle at the moment,</i>

00:21:13.420 --> 00:21:16.440
<i>but all that matters is that 
I win in the very end.</i>

00:21:16.920 --> 00:21:18.200
<i>I will not lose.</i>

00:21:18.930 --> 00:21:23.330
<i>All ships, focus on destroying individual 
crafts until I give further orders.</i>

00:21:23.330 --> 00:21:24.400
<i>That is all.</i>

00:21:26.820 --> 00:21:28.740
"I will not lose"...

00:21:29.340 --> 00:21:32.800
"Obey my orders, and you 
will be saved," eh?

00:21:33.410 --> 00:21:37.660
I never knew the rebel forces had 
such a braggart among their ranks.

00:21:38.260 --> 00:21:42.480
How does he intend to turn his 
disadvantage around at this stage?

00:21:43.200 --> 00:21:44.550
Well, no matter.

00:21:45.200 --> 00:21:48.580
Let's see what he's got, Kircheis.

00:21:49.340 --> 00:21:50.190
Yes.

00:21:51.110 --> 00:21:52.750
Reorganize the battle lines.

00:21:52.750 --> 00:21:56.580
Instruct all fleets to move 
into a spindle formation.

00:21:56.580 --> 00:21:58.180
Do you understand why?

00:21:58.820 --> 00:22:01.200
You intend to break through their center.

00:22:01.200 --> 00:22:03.710
That's right. I knew you'd get it.

00:22:31.410 --> 00:22:33.700
Compiling data from patrol crafts.

00:22:33.700 --> 00:22:34.970
Operating in real time.

00:22:36.280 --> 00:22:38.040
It appears we've won.

00:22:38.040 --> 00:22:39.030
Yes.

00:22:46.860 --> 00:22:48.330
Is something the matter?

00:22:50.690 --> 00:22:52.070
Reinhardt?

00:22:52.780 --> 00:22:55.150
It's strange. Something isn't right.

00:22:55.770 --> 00:22:59.330
We're winning. There's no doubt about that.

00:23:00.760 --> 00:23:01.600
But...

00:23:07.960 --> 00:23:09.140
No!

00:24:50.010 --> 00:25:00.010
<b>Episode 2</b>

00:24:50.010 --> 00:25:00.010
<b>The Battle of Astarte</b>

00:24:50.510 --> 00:24:55.210
<i>Next time on </i>Legend of 
 the Galactic Heroes - Die Neue These<i>,</i>

00:24:55.210 --> 00:24:58.840
<i>episode two: "The Battle of Astarte."</i>
